sim6809: a headless MC6809 simulator, used by the regression tests to
run test programs.

These sources are copied unchanged from the sim/ directory of the
plm09 project (https://github.com/retrotinker/plm09), version 0.4.2,
which is under the MIT license (see LICENSE in this directory). Its
user manual is docs/sim6809.md in that project.

"make check" builds it; to update it, copy the sim/*.c and sim/*.h
files from a newer plm09 release and change the version number in the
sim6809 rule in the top-level Makefile.

Programs talk to it through an I/O block at $FF00: a byte written to
$FF00 is printed, a byte written to $FF02 stops the simulator with that
byte as its exit status, and $FF04/$FF05 print a 16-bit number.
tests/src/simcrt0.s uses these for the test programs.
